        "original_id": "ae064495-0182-5771-bde5-3c90bea516b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dog breeds: Havanese, Black Mouth Cur, Poodle\n- Places: Cuba, Havana, Southern United States\n- Concepts: Bichon type, cording, dog showing\n\nFacts:\n- The Havanese is a breed of Bichon type.\n- The Havanese is the national dog of Cuba.\n- The Havanese was developed from the now extinct Blanquito de la Habana, which means \"little white dog of Havana.\"\n- Havana Silk Dogs was originally another name for the Blanquito de la Habana.\n- The Black Mouth Cur is a hunting and cattle dog from the Southern United States.\n- The Havanese is occasionally corded for showing.\n- The Poodle is also occasionally corded for showing.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
